if __name__=='__main__':
 g1=load('phase8b-G1-verdict.json');stats=load('phase8b-core-statistics.json');campaign=load('phase8b-combined-campaign-receipt.json');cases=load('phase8b-locked-campaign-cases.json');adapter=load('phase8b-P2-adapter-training-freeze.json');mass=stats['mass'];lines=['# Phase8B G1–G3 core experiments','', 'Status: actual core campaign completed; scientific comparisons below are descriptive/exploratory. Q8.4 and manuscript figures/TeX/PDF remain unstarted.','', '## Scope and data roles','', 'Five online specialists share a frozen numerical response tool. External WOFOST81-SNOMIN alone supplies native mechanistic outcomes and daily C/N ledgers. This is a simulator study, not field validation or an operational weather forecast. Agent count has no causal performance claim; the identical monolithic numerical controller is bit-for-bit equivalent.','', 'P1 uses TRAIN1995–2009, exposed Dev2010–2014 and an adaptive-reused temporal benchmark. Report52 Former-Held-Out and7 Public-Reused NASA site-years separately. WUR7 public historical site-years use WUR CSV observed weather, a NASA TRAIN numerical backbone/forecast model and NASA TRAIN climate analog branches. The climate module retains its imported original regional_weather alias; only engine construction is patched to WUR. This is a limited nine-policy weather-transfer stratum, not the full P1 control/ablation matrix or exact original CEA replication. See phase8b-WUR-source-binding-proof.json. NASA and WUR are never pooled.','', 'Historical Phase7 Satellite_bridge remains0%on each corresponding40Former/4Public cohort in both schemes, with actual subset counts saved in phase8b-Phase7-historical-cohort-reference.json; its imputation interface is not the current matched world-model policy. P2 is explicitly retrospective nested LOYO/LORO cross-fitting:44 site-years per scheme,40 Former-Held-Out and4 Public-Reused NL. Outer held labels never fit transformations, priors, regression heads, applicability thresholds or inner calibration. LOYO and LORO are separate analyses, not88 independent farms. The frozen P1 backbone is not updated and was trained on all five regions in1995–2009; LORO therefore tests adapter transfer conditional on that backbone, not whole-system zero-shot regional generalization. Annual t-1 vectors are admissible only after their calendar-year end precedes the decision date; no historical product release availability is claimed.','', '## G1 actual pass and limits','', 'Both registered13155-parameter architectures passed all prespecified G1 gates in both information tracks. First-registered MLP remained primary. No Dev-driven architecture/hyperparameter/checkpoint search followed. Exact G1 implementation is archived in phase8b-G1-source-snapshot/.','', '|Track/model|90% crossyear Dev coverage|Within-prefix regret EUR/ha|ExtraTrees regret EUR/ha|','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
 for name,r in g1['results'].items():
  lines.append(f"|{name}|{pct(r['Dev_crossyear_macro_90pct_coverage'])}|{r['partial_profit_ranking_regret_EUR_ha']:.3f}|{r['ExtraTrees_regret_EUR_ha']:.3f}|")
 lines+=['','See PHASE8B_G1_GATE_REPORT.md and phase8b-G1-verdict.json for full BSS against both TRAIN climatology and fold-matched ExtraTrees at all four caps. Coverage is retrospective leave-one-Dev-year-out calibration verification, not prospective or regionwise coverage. Conditional TRAIN OOF residuals use realized TRAIN scenario descriptors; they are not operational forecastOOF. The literal BSS event is S_N<=cap; two-sided surplus and joint NUE compliance are reported separately.','', 'TRAIN physical decoding is an association audit only. High global reconstruction can reflect region structure; within-region N-loss decodability must be read from the full TRAIN audit. It does not prove causal understanding of64 spatial axes.','', '## G2 and G3 realized metrics','', '|Benchmark|Source|Cohort|Scheme|Track|Policy|Cap|N price multiplier|Subsidy EUR/ha|Site-years|Region-equal joint|Pooled joint|Profit EUR/ha|Native N loss kg/ha|','|---|---|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 primary=[]
