 for s in stats['summary']:
  m=s['region_equal'];lines.append(f"|{s['benchmark']}|{s['source']}|{s['cohort']}|{s['scheme']}|{s['track']}|{s['policy']}|{s['cap']}|{s['price_multiplier']}|{s['subsidy']}|{s['site_years']}|{pct(m['joint'])}|{pct(s['pooled']['joint'])}|{m['partial_profit']:.2f}|{m['Native_N_loss']:.3f}|")
 lines+=['','All individual-region rates, executed N, NUE, yield, surplus, profit, native loss and Tier1/2/3 are saved in phase8b-core-statistics.json; annual observations and within-case PPO seed means are in phase8b-case-metrics-seed-averaged.csv. Native descriptive NL references have no shared Tier labels. Their clocks/action budgets differ and are not called fully matched. Historical published/reported21.8788/23.5657/40/28.57% remain historical references, not reproduced results. Frozen v6/PPO actors here use the common v8 tail-safety guard, explicitly a transfer.','', 'P1 Static-Soil DL is the Sensorless TreeMLP alias; no duplicate native physics was launched. P1 contains no64-D spatial prior. GroupA therefore spans P1 numerical families and P2 low-rank prior controls. P2 controls receive the same outer-label cohort and inner calibration protocol; all34986prepared rows pass the annual-end timing predicate; China has fewer legal rows because basal171restricts remaining nominal doses. Prior OOD rejection and effective radii are explicitly logged; LORO may reduce to frozen-backbone predictions with calibration-only differences. Pure-Weather excludes static soil and privileged telemetry.','', 'GroupB tests tree, soft penalties, initial-plan frozen Open-Loop343 and current-action greedy80/80 continuation. Hard monolithic and five-specialist versions are exact numeric aliases; no claimed benefit from additional agent names. GroupC removes only climate branches on TRAIN-quantile wet/dry cases, only surplus constraints at caps25/35, or only NUE/dynamic valuation at price2x and TRAIN-selected subsidy. This is not the90-cell stress surface. Soft Tier1 means selection by soft score with hard Eco/NUE targets disabled; it is not an active hard-constraint tier or realized-compliance claim. Soft Tier3 means OOD zero. Numeric counts are unchanged and tier_label_semantics is explicit in every statistics row. Fourteen of177open-loop stage traces have null applicability/score/radius/hash metadata on the later-stage OOD-zero path; dose0andTier3are recorded correctly, and those original traces remain immutable.','', 'The selected50EUR/ha subsidy is the first prespecified candidate changing any TRAIN full three-stage plan. It is an experimental stress magnitude, not a minimum subsidy achieving compliance, an enacted policy, or proof of policy success. Legacy v6 strict null subsidy thresholds remain untouched.','', '## Prior usage and actual fallback', '', 'All P2 decisions log prior acceptance, annual-end admissibility, prior OOD and effective calibration radius. Per-episode counts are in phase8b-core-statistics.json prior_usage. A rejected prior yields the frozen backbone, so any difference attributable only to fallback radii is not evidence that spatial information improved decisions. In particular LORO conditions on a backbone already trained in all five regions.', '', '## Paired inference and physical ceilings','', 'Paired bootstrap B5000, seed20261115 resamples site-years after averaging all three PPO seeds within each case. Exact two-sided sign and Wilcoxon tests, ties, effective nonzero n and full-family Holm adjustment are saved in phase8b-core-statistics.json. NL NASA n5 has minimum exact two-sided sign p=.0625. Wilcoxon uses exact dynamic-programming counts of all2^n_eff signed-rank allocations with average tied ranks and zeros removed. Numeric tie tolerances were frozen before outcomes. These exploratory tests assume exchangeable independent site-year differences; signed-rank inference also requires a symmetric null difference distribution.','', 'Old finite-GRID physical feasibility ceilings are AU11/11, US12/12, NL4/5 NASA, FR1/12 and CN0/12 with basal171kg/ha. They apply to specified simulated calendars/physics and discrete interventions, not a continuous field oracle. Failure on CN/FR cannot be explained away as model tuning opportunity on held labels.','', '## Verification, failure preservation and reproducibility','', f"The original attempt completed6seasons then stopped on2incomplete legacy-wrapper failures. Epoch28 authorized only2incomplete restarts plus2009unstarted cases. Recovery1 was not a clean pass: it saved1454of2011expected results, then all8workers exited1 and the supervisor failed its final completion assertion after4WUR pre-integration constructor errors. Recovery2 completed557of557missing IDs with all8worker exits0. The disjoint union is6+1454+557=2017, including exactly2authorized incomplete-season restarts. Earlier receipts, failed assertions and both old STOP markers remain intact. Four additional WUR constructor failures occurred before physical integration and were repaired by retaining the identical CSV data in a native-compatible provider subclass. Those startup records remain preserved. The original two incomplete physical prefixes ended before serialized external daily audit; only completed, scored seasons enter the2017-run audit. The combined audit saved{campaign['result_count']}of{campaign['expected']}native episodes. Daily conservation passed on all{mass['native_runs']}runs/{mass['daily_records']}daily records: max|N|={mass['max_N']:.12g}kg/ha below1e-10; max|C|={mass['max_C']:.12g}kg/ha below1e-9.", '', 'Thirty actual online-controller target-future perturbations passed in both tracks with actual frozen in-domain numerical models. Positive-control past weather changes invalidate the response cache. The target season was excluded from TRAIN analogs. An additional30actual nonzero Stage2-action perturbations passed both tracks. Tests do not rely on trivial OOD-zero actions.','', f"P2 saved{adapter['fit_count']}outer-fold adapter fits with inner year exclusions, fixed ranks<=4 and Ridgealpha10. Full fold membership, hashes and calibration radii are saved in phase8b-P2-adapter-training-freeze.json. Raw64 numeric vectors remain private binary tool artifacts and never enter specialist messages or human decision rules.", '', 'The P2 preprocessing assertion caught an omitted basal171 budget filter before adapter weights/native evaluation. Superseded arrays and the failed fit log are retained; the corrected predicate is committed N plus remaining nominal doses<=220. No outcome-based model/hyperparameter selection resulted.','', 'See canonical test receipt, external review originals/reconciliation, preservation receipts and final runtime pins for verified commands/SHAs. Review availability and actual served providers must be reported from their actual receipts, never inferred from dispatch.','']
 rendered='\n'.join(lines)
 rendered=rendered.replace('## Scope and data roles',(P/'phase8b-approved-verdict-text.md').read_text()+'## Scope and data roles',1)
